      "body": "# App Monetization & Pricing Models for Solo Developers\n\n## Overview\nChoosing the appropriate monetization structure directly determines product adoption, user retention, and long-term recurring revenue for solo applications and tools.\n\n---\n\n## Monetization Frameworks\n\n### 1. Freemium with Lifetime Pro Unlock\n* **Mechanism**: Core utility is free with reasonable usage limits. Advanced power tools (high-res exports, unlimited cloud sync, custom palettes) require a one-time In-App Purchase (IAP).\n* **Best For**: Creative utilities, pattern generators, standalone tools (e.g., BlanketDesignGenerator).\n* **Advantage**: High user goodwill, low churn resistance compared to subscription fatigue.\n\n### 2. Tiered Subscription (Monthly / Annual)\n* **Mechanism**: Low entry price ($2.99/mo or $19.99/yr) unlocking continuous cloud synchronization, premium AI features, or continuous database updates.\n* **Best For**: Cloud-heavy apps with ongoing server compute/API costs (e.g., automated inventory tracking, smart home cloud connectors).\n\n### 3. Rewarded Video Ads / Non-Intrusive Banners\n* **Mechanism**: Users can optionally watch a 15-30s ad to unlock a temporary premium action (e.g., generate 5 extra patterns or export a PDF).\n* **Best For**: Casual, broad audience apps where direct payment conversion is under 3%."
