      "body": "\ufeff---\ntitle: \"Business & Strategy Index\"\ndomain: \"business-and-strategy\"\ncategory: \"general\"\ntype: \"hub\"\ntags: [\"business\", \"strategy\", \"market-intelligence\", \"competitive-analysis\", \"index\"]\ncreated: 2026-08-18\nupdated: 2026-08-18\nstatus: active\nsummary: \"Map of Content for market intelligence, competitive analysis, positioning, and go-to-market strategy relevant to BA Insight and the SmartHub platform.\"\n---\n\n# Business & Strategy\n\nThis domain captures market intelligence, competitor and vendor observations, product positioning, and go-to-market strategy \u2014 the commercial context that shapes BA Insight's technical roadmap.\n\n---\n\n## Core Knowledge Notes\n\n| Note | Type | Summary |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [LegalTech Talk 2026: Market & Competitor Intelligence](legaltech-talk-2026.md) | investigation | Conference readout: governed AI over raw capability, agentic orchestration as a category, competitor intel (Legora, Leah, Autologyx, DeepJudge, iManage MCP), and positioning implications for BA Insight. |\n\n---\n\n## Operating Principles\n1. **Market language over feature language** \u2014 track how the market frames value (\"governed AI work\", \"knowledge activation\", \"agentic orchestration\"), not just feature parity.\n2. **Positioning follows capability** \u2014 competitive intel should feed back into roadmap and demo storytelling, not sit in isolation.\n3. **Evidence-based** \u2014 attribute observations to their source event/vendor and date; distinguish confirmed intel from inference.\n"
