      "body": "\ufeff---\ntitle: \"SmartHub UI Framework & Layouts\"\ndomain: \"smarthub\"\ncategory: \"work\"\ntype: \"architecture\"\ntags: [\"smarthub\", \"ui-framework\", \"layouts\", \"ui-editor\", \"templating\", \"javascript\"]\ncreated: 2026-08-18\nupdated: 2026-08-18\nstatus: active\nsummary: \"Architecture of the SmartHub UI framework, covering page lifecycles, module registration, UI Editor customization, Handlebars templates, and responsive layouts.\"\nrelated:\n  - \"[[INDEX]]\"\n  - \"[[advanced-search-module.md]]\"\n  - \"[[faceted-filtering-and-refiners.md]]\"\n  - \"[[content-containers-module.md]]\"\n---\n\n# SmartHub UI Framework & Layouts\n\nSmartHub's user interface is built on a modular, client-side rendering architecture utilizing vanilla JavaScript (ES5/ES6 compatibility), jQuery, Handlebars-based templating, and CSS grid/flexbox layouts. It runs without server-side ASPX rendering requirements.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Page Lifecycle & Module Execution\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant Browser as Browser Client\n    participant Core as SmartHub Core (SH.js)\n    participant Config as CustomSettings.js\n    participant Service as REST Search Service\n    participant DOM as Page DOM\n\n    Browser->>Core: Load HTML page (e.g. Results.html)\n    Core->>Config: Initialize SH.DefaultSettings & Merge CustomSettings\n    Core->>Core: Instantiate registered modules (SearchBox, Refiners, Results, Previews)\n    Core->>Service: Dispatch search query payload\n    Service-->>Core: Return JSON SearchResponse\n    Core->>DOM: Render templates via Handlebars into container elements\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Directory Structure & Module Layout\n\nSmartHub web applications are structured with clear separation between core framework modules and site-specific customizations:\n\n```\nSmartHub/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 app/                              # Core JS libraries & runtime\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 js/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SH.js                     # Core framework orchestrator\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SH.SearchService.js       # REST client & query builder\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 DefaultSettings.js        # Global defaults across all modules\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 css/                          # Core stylesheets\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 modules/                          # Pluggable functional modules\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 AdvancedSearch/               # Parametric search modal\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SearchBox/                    # Query input, autocomplete & NLQ\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SearchResults/                # Result list, cards & metadata badges\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 Refiners/                     # Faceted filters, sliders, taxonomy trees\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ContentContainers/            # Federated blended result containers\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SmartPreviews/                # In-line document preview viewer\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 UserRating/                   # Document feedback & rating widget\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 QueryHistory/                 # Recent searches & saved query alerts\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 templates/                        # Global Handlebars templates\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 CustomPages/                      # Site-specific custom pages & settings\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 CustomResults.html\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 CustomSettings.js\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 index.html                        # Home / landing search page\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. UI Editor (Live Visual & Code Customization)\n\nThe **UI Editor** is an administrative tool embedded within SmartHub (`/UIEditor.html` or Administration menu) allowing real-time modification of search interfaces:\n\n### Operational Modes\n1. **Basic / Visual Mode**:\n   - Drag-and-drop module layout restructuring (reordering refiners, search boxes, result cards).\n   - Theme and brand color selection, logo uploading, typography toggles.\n2. **Advanced Settings Mode**:\n   - Direct JSON/JavaScript object editing of module configuration blocks (e.g., `SH.SearchResults.CustomSettings`, `SH.Refiners.CustomSettings`).\n   - Live preview pane rendering immediate test queries against backend engines.\n\n### Safe Customization Rules\n- **Never edit core files in `/modules/` or `/app/` directly.** Updates and patches will overwrite core files.\n- Always clone default templates to `CustomPages/` or define overrides in `CustomSettings.js`.\n- Always verify DOM null-checks before executing custom jQuery/JS extensions.\n"
